        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(handoff): skip orchestrator framing for solo agents without subagents",
        "body": "Fixes #102628\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`buildHierarchyReinforcementMessage` unconditionally claimed \"You are the new LEADER (Orchestrator)\" and showed \"ACTIVE SUBORDINATE UNITS: None active.\" even when the agent had no subagents. This reliably confused models (observed on Claude Opus 4.7) into inventing subordinates or fabricating orchestrator context after quota-suspension/failover recovery.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen `activeSubagents` is empty, the message now simply tells the model to review current state and continue instead of presenting orchestrator/subordinate framing that has no referent.\n\n## Evidence\n- `git diff --check` clean\n- Single file change: `src/auto-reply/handoff-summarizer.ts` (15 insertions, 9 deletions)",
